.TH JETWEB 7 "May 2026" "v1.0" "Sovereign Mesh Manual"
.SH NAME
jetweb \- Retroactive timeline refactoring and re-mining engine
.SH DESCRIPTION
The **JetWeb Time Machine** is a state-collapse hard-fork mechanism for the Sovereign Mesh. It allows supervisors to override past swarm decisions and programmatically recalculate the immutable ledger history.
.SH OPERATIONAL MECHANICS
When a suboptimal or malicious decision is identified at Block \fBT\fR, the engine rewrites history by performing an instantaneous cascade re-mining:
.IP 1.
\fBBlock Targeting:\fR Locks the ledger from index 1 to N.
.IP 2.
\fBPayload Mutation:\fR Overwrites the payload and consensus votes of the target block.
.IP 3.
\fBHash Recalculation:\fR Recomputes the SHA-256 signature for the modified block.
.IP 4.
\fBCascade Re-mining:\fR Updates every subsequent block's \fBprevious_hash\fR and unique signature to maintain cryptographic integrity.
.IP 5.
\fBState Tree Replay:\fR Clears active operational memory and replays the new ledger to build a harmonized state.
.SH FORENSICS
Every Time Machine override is logged as a ticket in the \fBTime-Machine\fR queue, providing full accountability for timeline bifurcations.
.SH SEE ALSO
\fBsovereign-mesh\fR(7), \fBstarbirth\fR(7)
